{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773875717,"nonce":"pY7H5niLoGnon73drRFg9T8Esnw=","title":"Experiment: work a day with blank/minimal CLAUDE.md to get parallax on current conventions","message":"Idea: spend a day working with a blank or near-blank CLAUDE.md to see what Claude does naturally, without accumulated conventions shaping its behavior. The goal is parallax — discovering which conventions are load-bearing vs. cargo-cult, and whether any current rules are actively harmful or just assumed-good.\n\nTwo variants worth trying:\n\n**Variant A — fully blank:**\nRemove or stub out CLAUDE.md entirely for a day. See what Claude does without guidance. What does it get right by default? What goes wrong immediately? What does it reinvent from scratch? This would likely break Mandible integration (no auth queue awareness, no hook knowledge, no worktree tooling). So probably only viable for work in repos that are less tightly integrated with Mandible.\n\n**Variant B — tools-aware but non-prescriptive:**\nKeep CLAUDE.md aware of available tools (mandible, wt, git-bug, agent-commit, etc.) and the protected-branch merge requirement (auth request mandatory), but remove all the \"always do X\", \"never do Y\", \"when Z do W\" behavioral directives. Let Claude make its own decisions about workflow, commit style, parallelization, memory, etc. This is the more useful experiment since Mandible can still function.\n\nQuestions this experiment would answer:\n- Which conventions does Claude arrive at independently vs. need to be told?\n- Which rules exist because Claude got it wrong once and we overfit on that incident?\n- Are there better approaches Claude would find if not constrained?\n- Is the current CLAUDE.md length (and resulting context cost) justified?\n\nSuggested approach: create a branch of dotfiles with a stripped CLAUDE.md (Variant B), use it for a real work session, then compare behavior and write up findings. Could also be run as a labmode experiment with explicit before/after notes.\n\nNote: auth request convention probably must stay regardless — it is a hard safety requirement, not a workflow preference.","files":null}]}